      "data": {
        "text": "**Initiating Transcription Process**\n\nI'm now implementing `submit_transcription.py`. It'll leverage `get_speech_client` from `speech_client.py` to submit audio files for batch transcription. I'm focused on defining a function that accepts the audio URI and configuration parameters, handling the call to the Google Cloud Speech-to-Text API. My goal is to streamline the process.\n\n\n**Refining Implementation Strategy**\n\nI'm refining the implementation of `submit_transcription.py` and aiming for greater efficiency. The function in question now uses the `long_running_recognize` method directly. I am keeping the initial design as simple as possible, with the audio assumed to be in a GCS bucket, for now.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789830108295,
          "start": 1789830105828
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0ba300ae4001GJFwTKAA6My4ng",
